{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And when you sell a sale, etc. — do not wrong.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained: this is monetary oppression, and it comes to warn against oppression, to say: when you sell or purchase land, know how many years there are until the Jubilee; and according to the years, the seller shall sell and the buyer shall purchase, since in the end it will return to him in the year of the Jubilee. And if there are few years and he sells it for a high price, then the buyer has been wronged; and if there are many years and he consumes many harvests from it, then the seller has been wronged. Therefore one must buy it according to the time. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: וכי תמכרו ממכר לעמיתך — when you sell, sell to your fellow Israelite; או קנה מיד עמיתך — or if you come to purchase, purchase from your fellow Israelite." "<b>And the reason</b> this passage is adjoined to the passage of the Sabbatical year and the Jubilee — they said in the Midrash that it is a warning to Israel that they should fulfill the commandments of the Sabbatical years and the Jubilees. For thus they said: If a person did not keep the commandment of the Sabbatical year and the Jubilee, in the end he sells his movable property, as it is said: וכי תמכרו ממכר לעמיתך או קנה מיד עמיתך — a thing acquired from hand to hand, these are movable goods. If he repented, well; and if not, in the end he sells his field, as it is said: וכי ימוך אחיך ומכר מאחזתו. If he repented, well; and if not, in the end he sells his house, as it is said: ואיש כי ימכור בית מושב. If he repented, well; and if not, he goes about begging at the doors, as it is said: וכי ימוך אחיך ומטה ידו עמך. If he repented, well; and if not, in the end he sells himself, as it is said: וכי ימוך אחיך ונמכר לך. If he repented, well; and if not, in the end he is sold to a gentile, as it is said: ונמכר לגר תושב עמך או לעקר משפחת גר. Thus far in the Midrash. And so we find that what befell Israel because they did not keep the Sabbatical year was as it is said (Jeremiah 34:11): וישיבו את העבדים ואת השפחות אשר שלחו חפשים ויכבשום לעבדים ולשפחות. And as punishment for this they were sold to the Chaldeans in the days of Zedekiah, when the Temple was destroyed — as it is written (2 Chronicles 36:17): ויעל עליהם את מלך כשדים ויהרוג בחוריהם בחרב בבית מקדשם ולא חמל על בחור ובתולה וזקן וישש הכל נתן בידו, and all the vessels of the house of HaElohim, the great and the small, and the treasuries of the house of HaShem and the treasuries of the king and his officers — all of it he brought to Babylon."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:20.822625988Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}